    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d462-a6">

                <pb facs="0550" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg468"/>

                <head>General Weitzel to General Crawford</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Headquarters District of the Rio
                                Grande, Brownsville, Texas,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-01-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 2, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">General:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your communication of yesterday.</p>
                <p>I have, notified General Mejia of the opinion which I firmly believe my
                    government holds on that subject, and have entered solemn protest in writing
                    against the act. General Mejia replies that he is obliged to obey the orders of
                    his government. I will notify my superiors of this; but I have positive, written
                    orders not to commence hostilities without instructions so to do.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>G. WEITZEL, <hi rendition="#italic">Major General
                        Commanding.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>R. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clay Crawford, General of Division, Army of
                            Mexico.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
